      "quality_note": "DELIBERATELY ABSENT, not unmeasured. Measured 2026-08-25 per timepoint against the *_preprocessed.npy volumes the fit consumed (global PSNR 35.57/30.03/19.65/21.11 dB and foreground 30.17/13.12/9.52/8.51 dB at t0/t100/t200/t300), and the foreground figures are NOT publishable: Otsu drifts 13.3x over the recording (0.0135 -> 0.1795), so 'foreground' is a different region at every timepoint. At t0 the low threshold admits 26.4% of a nearly-empty one-cell embryo, inflating that end, so the apparent trend mixes real quality loss with threshold drift. Real quality DOES fall across the recording -- MAX_SPLATS is a fixed 22,000 per timepoint while the embryo goes from one cell to hundreds of nuclei -- but a stable mask is needed to say by how much. Template: the zebrafish demo's fixed component-based definition (voxels inside 6-connected components of >= 27 voxels in the raw frame), which does not move with image content."
