      "quality_note": "REFIT 2026-08-25 from Janelia's public H5J (sha256 189595b1...) and scored on the VOXEL GRID before any transform, with --image-min 1 matching the background level every box subtracted. Scoring after the rotate-y/scale/rotate-z chain is invalid (droso lost 16 dB that way), and the fit could not stamp itself: full-volume scoring peaks at ~96 GiB against a 22.4 GiB budget, so `gsplat compare` was run on the written archive as the fitter advised. NOTE this is a NEW fit, not a re-measurement of the previously shipped archive: 508,371 splats against 653,759, from the same cal_h5j.json, the same 75-box content plan (47 non-empty) and the same --floor auto. The figures therefore describe THIS archive. Global PSNR 60.13 dB is near-meaningless here (99.93% of voxels are empty); the foreground figure is the one that says whether the neurites survived. Cross-check: cal_h5j.json's held-out foreground peaked at 32.63 dB on the densest 320^3 region, so 36.00 dB whole-volume with more splats is consistent."
